      "postID": "5a04ee60658a945fe73a426a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "+1 to the showcase channel. One for worlds would be pretty swell too. It'd make discovering new worlds easier as you wouldn't have to go through the arduous process of logging in, browsing through the worlds list, and then waiting for it to download on the client.\n\nI'm not sure I like the idea of making a 'beginners' or 'questions' channel as they usually become too imbalanced with many people asking questions, but few people providing actual answers.\n\nAvatars as it is now is great for beginners because they can get answers quickly there - with the downside being that it becomes harder to discuss other things besides the questions. That said, if questions were separated by topic, they might become a bit easier to manage.\n\nOne thing I'd like to see is Avatars split up between Blender stuff and Unity stuff. That way, modelling topics like decimation or rigging could be discussed in one place while shaders, overrides, and scripting could be discussed in another.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
